== Malnutrition
=== Common Nutritional Disorders of BD
- Protein energy malnutrition (PEM)
- Micronutrient deficiency-related malnutrition
  - Micronutrients with greatest public health importance: Vit A, Iron, Iodine, Zinc
  - Other micronutrients: Vit B, C, D, Folic acid, Calcium, etc.
=== Aetiology and risk factors
 - Immediate causes
   - Inadequate dietary intake (energy and protein), poor feeding practices
   - Recurrent or chronic infections (diarrhoea, pneumonia, TB, HIV)
 - Underlying determinants
   - Food insecurity, poverty, maternal malnutrition, low birth weight
   - Inadequate weaning foods, poor sanitation, limited access to healthcare
 - Contributing medical factors
   - Malabsorption (celiac disease, chronic diarrhoea), chronic renal or cardiac disease
 - Prevention/Programmatic
   - Exclusive breastfeeding for 6 months, appropriate complementary feeding, micronutrient supplementation, immunization and infection control
=== Older classification
- Underweight → Marasmus (no oedema)
- Kwashiorkor → oedema present
- Marasmic-kwashiorkor → both
=== Malnutrition classification parameters
- Weight for age
- Weight for height %
- Height for age %
- MUAC
- Oedema
=== WHO criteria of SAM
- Weight for height < –3 Z-score (or < 70% of median)
- MUAC < 115 mm (for children 6–60 months)
- Bilateral pitting oedema (Kwashiorkor)
=== Sakir tape use and interpretation
- Use: MUAC tape (usually red/yellow/green zones)
- Measurement: mid-upper arm circumference on left arm, midpoint between acromion and olecranon
- Interpretation (6–60 months):
  - Green (≥125 mm): Normal
  - Yellow (115–124 mm): Moderate acute malnutrition / at risk
  - Red (< 115 mm): SAM
